  "result": "I added `clamp(cents, low, high)` to the end of `shop/money.py` and wrote tests for it. The full test suite passes: 13 tests, all OK, run with `python3 -m unittest discover` (plain `python` isn't installed here).\n\n- **`clamp`** returns `low` if `cents` is below `low`, `high` if it's above `high`, and `cents` otherwise. If `low` is greater than `high` it raises `ValueError` with a message showing both values.\n- **Tests:** There was no test file for `money.py`, so I created `tests/test_money.py` using `unittest`, like the other test files. It covers:\n  - a value inside the range\n  - values below `low` and above `high`\n  - values exactly equal to each bound\n  - `low == high`\n  - the `ValueError` case\n\nNothing is committed yet.",
